  <h2>What Is Dividend Investing?</h2>
  <p>Dividend investing is a strategy where you buy shares of companies that regularly distribute a portion of their profits to shareholders. Unlike growth investing, dividend investing focuses on generating consistent cash income from your holdings.</p>
  <blockquote>Over the last 100 years, dividends contributed roughly 40% of the S&P 500's total return. Reinvesting those dividends is where the real magic happens.</blockquote>
